From: Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>
Subject: tests: build the unit tests with the same SSL configuration as the library

tests/gtest/tests/CMakeLists.txt hardcodes QT_NO_SSL, while the library is
built with qmqtt_SSL=ON by default.  QT_NO_SSL is not an implementation
detail: it removes three pure virtuals from the middle of
QMQTT::NetworkInterface and four from QMQTT::SocketInterface, so the mocks
compiled into the test binary get a different vtable layout than the libqmqtt
that binary links against.  libqmqtt then dispatches connectToHost() through a
slot the mock does not have and the suite dies in
ClientTest.connectToHostWillCallNetworkConnectToHost with SIGSEGV.

Use the same ${ssl_defs} the library target uses, so the tests follow the
qmqtt_SSL option instead of contradicting it.

--- qmqtt-1.0.7.orig/tests/gtest/tests/CMakeLists.txt
+++ qmqtt-1.0.7/tests/gtest/tests/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -47,7 +47,7 @@
 target_compile_definitions(qmqtt_tests
     PRIVATE
         QMQTT_LIBRARY_TESTS
-        QT_NO_SSL
+        ${ssl_defs}
 )
 
 # Set C++ standard
